{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The smart plug feels like a useful next purchase because it would let me control a lamp through the Echo devices I already use.",
    "The Blink doorbell connects my earlier interest in door alarms with my recent Alexa purchases, adding front-door alerts and two-way communication if installation works for my home."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Both Fire TV sticks fit my interests, but my recent 4K Max bundle already fills that need; another stick offers no clear purpose right now.",
    "The earbuds do not address a current need, and the stylus assumes I have a compatible iPad even though my history does not establish that.",
    "A larger Echo display and separate security cameras are interesting, but my recent Show 5 covers my display needs, and I would try the doorbell before expanding to other cameras."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Alexa purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to suggest more Alexa devices, even when they repeat functions I already have.",
    "My frequent electronics purchases seem to have been treated as interest in almost any electronic accessory, without a clear connection to equipment I use or a problem I need to solve."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases matter because they can satisfy a need: buying a Fire TV bundle or an Echo Show does not mean I immediately want another one.",
    "Purchases such as the Echo Show stand and Harmony replacement batteries suggest that accessories supporting equipment I already own can be more useful to me than another main device.",
    "I would expand home security one step at a time, starting with a doorbell whose installation requirements I can check before considering additional cameras."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my Alexa and home-electronics interests, but miss that I currently value useful additions to my setup more than duplicate devices or unrelated accessories."
}"}
